  "quote_spans": [
    {
      "chunk_id": 41,
      "char_start": 1411,
      "char_end": 1688,
      "text": "This new aspect of\nher had put him in doubt for a while, but it was not very long before he\nsatisfied himself that he understood what it meant; and that little\naffair with the tea-tray, that was set down to awkwardness by the\nothers, had quite a different significance for him"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": 52,
      "char_start": 899,
      "char_end": 1427,
      "text": "At the same time, as Elizabeth was not blind\nto the diplomacy of the house, she had soon perceived that of all the\nyoung ladies who came there, Marie Forstberg was the one who had the\nbest chance, and who indeed best deserved to be the young lieutenant's\nbride; and although she tried to believe that she was merely a resigned\nlooker-on herself, she seemed to feel every Sunday, when Marie Forstberg\ncame, that a certain disagreeable impression had grown up in her mind\nabout her during the week which it took some time to thaw"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": 53,
      "char_start": 0,
      "char_end": 335,
      "text": "pilot-and-his-wife\n\nMarie Forstberg couldn't help sometimes\nfixing her clear blue eyes searchingly upon her, to ascertain if there\nwas not some object underlying this communicativeness; but Elizabeth\nwould look so unconscious, as she stood there with her sleeves tucked\nup, busy with her work, that she dismissed the idea from her mind"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": 122,
      "char_start": 0,
      "char_end": 156,
      "text": "pilot-and-his-wife\n\nIf we are tempted to think otherwise, we have not penetrated to\nthe simple, childlike nature which underlies the sailor's rough\nexterior"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": 137,
      "char_start": 1022,
      "char_end": 1324,
      "text": "There was\nsomething almost imperious in Elizabeth's manner at times that made them\nfeel quite small beside her; and however careless she might be of the\n_convenances_ in her way of speaking to them, they had very soon found\nthat wherever she chose to draw the line, so far could they go and no\nfarther"
    }
  ],
